{"id": "EUVD-2026-103858", "enisaUuid": "cedd3e00-b93f-35de-90b5-bf22f2a1b7ea", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nUSB: cdc-acm: skip URB restart in port_shutdown if disconnected\n\nacm_port_shutdown() is called from the tty-port machinery whenever the\nlast user closes the port.  acm_disconnect() sets acm->disconnected and\ncalls tty_port_tty_vhangup(), which eventually triggers port_shutdown().\nAt that point acm_disconnect() has already called acm_poison_urbs() and\nis about to free the control and read URBs.\n\nHowever, acm_port_shutdown() unconditionally calls acm_unpoison_urbs()\nand, when the ALWAYS_POLL_CTRL quirk is set, immediately re-submits the\nctrlurb and all read URBs.  If the concurrent acm_disconnect() then\nfrees those URBs and their DMA buffers while they are in-flight, the\nresult is a use-after-free in acm_ctrl_irq() or acm_read_bulk_callback()\naccessing the freed DMA memory.\n\nFix by checking acm->disconnected after draining the delayed anchor and\nreturning early: if we are in a disconnect path the URBs must remain\npoisoned and must not be resubmitted.\n\nThe early return is placed after the delayed-anchor drain loop because\nthat loop only cancels write-side accounting (wb->use = false and\nautopm counter) and does not touch the hardware path.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d86775e79838d7d2e38ccf506a7d0f8e2dd4d5d0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9742905d9ed5bf23ebe4c100dec80b6bc50fb522", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0ed07b5bbb2d8fcef86810453216070691816e7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/420ca35af891d33522cc08504768ccd60a4c450a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc614d6bc991740d41d5a99ac7765c4b675dda88"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fp39-rj9v-7xc4", "CVE-2026-98773"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "076a32aa-f1e1-3787-9ca1-bb7fb0152c7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.175 <6.2"}, {"id": "173cf42e-d012-37f8-b71d-a01b7dcd0c29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.83 <6.12.113"}, {"id": "2aad04f1-315f-3b3b-8b41-aa6dc4db5fb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "603d5a7110832e10165d21f9a1486399457177de <9742905d9ed5bf23ebe4c100dec80b6bc50fb522"}, {"id": "2b49507b-7b22-36b0-8a76-b1807afc5a29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f58752ebcb35e156c85cd1a82d6579c7af3b9023 <dc614d6bc991740d41d5a99ac7765c4b675dda88"}, {"id": "4c717467-4b11-379f-8421-44d74e232f2f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "5323158f-d2f2-3b83-8aa9-c7395e63a174", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.24 <6.18.56"}, {"id": "580f1ce3-d41d-35be-88bf-2ec3b82d3f8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5f816208-ee91-3c69-bdde-fedce12b308f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8fb82e3555a7d56a05d8ef0edee9859f889c0860 <d86775e79838d7d2e38ccf506a7d0f8e2dd4d5d0"}, {"id": "64cefdf4-50e4-3ba6-bc1d-bdcb69efbb1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "6cc52331-b66c-30a2-ac45-3a3f709a4950", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5d29d7ff8679e5a525f22da467ba33c042e8029b <a0ed07b5bbb2d8fcef86810453216070691816e7"}, {"id": "7007ef32-94bc-3838-897c-c647bf83faf0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d826061aa64cb28089bf4c73e301dd7928662b84"}, {"id": "73617e15-5015-35ad-a8a7-c81332089a62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f77f10bc76c2da86b4248269472f6d971e37828b"}, {"id": "7e6b9b